<title>USA: General Acceptance Corp Q4 loss widens.</title>
<headline>General Acceptance Corp Q4 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>BLOOMINGTON, Ind. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	loss	    $1.23     loss	 $0.51</p>
<p> Net	loss	    7,400     loss	 3,100</p>
<p> Revs			    NA			 NA</p>
<p> Avg shrs			NA			 NA</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q1 1996 includes $4.7 million non-cash valuation reserve for deferred taxes. Excluding reserve, Q4 1996 net loss would be $2.7 million or $0.46 a share.  </p>
<p>		     YEAR</p>
<p> Shr	loss	    $1.51   profit	 $0.13</p>
<p> Net	loss	    9,081   profit	   717</p>
<p> Revs			30,968		   25,639</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   6,022		    5,639</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 total net revenues include $29.0 million in total finance revenues vs $25.2 million in 1995.</p>
<p>1996 net loss includes $4.7 million reserve for deferred taxes. Excluding reserve, 1996 net loss was $4.4 million or $0.73 a share.</p>
<p>1995 results pro forma, adjusted for income taxes for publicly traded company.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
